# AWS CLI Log Sync

## Process

- Configured AWS CLI for authenticated access to the isolated lab environment.
- Used `aws s3 sync` to download compressed CloudTrail JSON from Amazon S3.
- Parameterized the source S3 URI so account and bucket identifiers are not committed.
- Stored downloaded logs locally for Splunk ingestion and analysis; the download directory is ignored by Git.

## Usage

```bash
./automation/s3-log-sync.sh s3://YOUR-BUCKET/AWSLogs/YOUR-ACCOUNT/CloudTrail/ ./cloudtrail-logs
```

## Result

Automated batch collection of CloudTrail logs from S3 instead of downloading individual files.

## Insight

Using AWS CLI for log retrieval is more efficient and scalable than manual downloads.

This adds a cloud engineering component to the project and makes the logging workflow more realistic for production-style environments.
